WEBVTT

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.360
You've got to be kidding.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.840
Tell me there is some kind of sick punchline coming.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.520
Unfortunately, John, it's true.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:13.140
Great.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:15.440
Absolutely great.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.060
We must go after him.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.420
Now two pods out there would just compound the problem.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:21.490
No change in his course.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.950
He's accelerating away from Moya.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.530
Let's be anything but surprised.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:27.510
Our weakest link is often the smallest.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:28.570
Can't we do something?

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:29.830
He's about to exit the asteroid.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.660
Peacekeepers haven't spotted him yet, but they will shortly.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.240
Pilot, I shall attempt to contact him again.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:38.650
Rigel, please respond!

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.980
Your eminence, I beg you, respond!

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.870
Remember, Rigel, Maya's baby has weaponry!

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:52.030
Rigel's already too distant, and the asteroid blocker clears cell bones.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:53.980
Rigel, listen to me.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:57.510
Listen very, very carefully.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:00:59.980
He's got a...

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:07.060
What the hell did you just say?

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.520
Something about his corpse and her bodily function.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:12.870
Oh, that'll help.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.460
Rigel, what you are doing is wrong.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:16.640
To you, maybe.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.020
Rigel, they'll take your head off.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.120
Whatever deal you cut with them,

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.180
Kreis will never honor.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.160
Rigel, kill your engines, float dead.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:25.340
Maybe they won't spot you.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:26.580
Let's talk about this.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:28.300
And isn't that the whole point, Crichton?

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:29.970
That's all your people ever do?

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:47.410
is talk i am a dominar of action transport flying straight towards us makes no sense pity we can't

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:54.870
follow its trail back to the leviathan any other vessels in motion out there just our own

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:58.200
outbound marauder with the alien girl you adopted

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:03.020
Have you found my security officer assigned to watch her?

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:06.500
Why would the Hynerian be traveling alone?

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:17.140
Perhaps he wishes to become part of your collection.

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.620
This is just a game to you, isn't it?

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.820
I care a great deal about one thing.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:29.980
The knowledge...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.820
The knowledge of wormhole technology is the human Crichton holds locked in his memory.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:42.900
Sirs, this Aenarian royal was alone aboard the Leviathan transport.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:47.030
You want the Leviathan? The Leviathan gunship offspring?

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:49.030
The other escaped prisoners?

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:51.610
The defector Eryn Sun?

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:55.960
And especially, you want the one called Crichton?

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.940
Well, I want my freedom.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:28.860
interested. I'm Crichton, an astronaut. A radiation wave hit and I got shot through a wormhole. I'm lost in some distant part of the universe on a ship, a living ship full of strange alien lifeforms help me. Listen, please. Is there anybody out there who can hear me? I'm being hunted by an insane military commander in everything I can.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.710
I'm just looking for a way home.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:57.000
Wait now.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:03:59.970
Peacekeepers knew where we were.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:10.900
They'd be here already. Look, is it possible he's just stalling them for us? Right. Let's think this through. What do we know?

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:16.520
The map of this asteroid field you took from the botanist has allowed pilot to plot starburst path away from the peacekeepers.

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:22.740
Moya will not abandon her baby. He was too young to starburst on his own. Is there any way we can use the offspring's weaponry to our advantage?

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:29.360
Well against the command carrier until he's fully grown, it'll be like throwing stones. I'll tell you this for free. I will not be taken alive.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.780
I've been in the goddamn chair, and I am not going back in it.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.220
I know of the concept, but there is no luxant word for it.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:35.400
Suicide?

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.560
I am not talking about suicide.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.590
But it doesn't look like we're going to get out of this one,

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.710
and if we're going to go down, I want to go down swinging.

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:44.390
Then we shall do so together.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:47.590
Oh, just to be in the warm glow of all this testosterone.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.450
The smaller ship Creighton Scorpius will send

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:52.170
can overpower us effortlessly.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:53.510
Okay, what do we see?

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:56.830
Rigel flew that transport right into their ship.

00:04:57.390 --> 00:04:59.230
Presumably screaming, I surrender all the way.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:04:59.970
Yeah, but what if one of us...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.420
of us did the same thing but at the last second veered off straight into the bridge a trojan horse

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:08.040
won't cripple their operations and what if the transport is loaded down with explosives

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:12.540
what if we blow the holy hell out of their nerves and would that buy us enough time

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:29.370
for the rest of us to get away that's for my third stomach that's what happens you see by the time

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:29.790
it's full

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:31.230
First one's empty again.

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:36.700
Dominar Rachel, my gimmick base is but a short distance away.

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:44.660
Once seated in my aurora chair, your hunger pangs will be the least of your discomforts.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:48.120
With all due respect, wrong.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:50.720
You won't get anything out of me that way.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:51.730
Ask him.

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:54.490
My physiology won't tolerate it.

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:55.870
You'd be dead almost instantly.

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:58.640
No need to travel to accommodate that.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:05:59.980
Look, if I were...

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:02.320
afraid I wouldn't have come, would I?

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:04.610
Pass the Tony Mollis, please.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:11.830
I believe your offer

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:15.250
was the capture of John Crichton

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:18.980
in exchange for your own freedom.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:20.860
And the Leviathan and the...

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.120
Insignificant, Captain.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:26.730
A simple deal to which I agree.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:28.370
Hardly simple.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:29.970
I also require...

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:36.980
a ship qualified crew negotiable currency a map to my home world and a full part you're lying

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:42.460
all right i could forgo the cash you're lying about why you're here no i'm not you're wasting

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:52.980
our time imprison him we will capture the others in due course i don't think so look i know him

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:55.890
john crichton will not be taken alive

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.000
Now he's telling the truth.

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:07.920
And are you willing to help me capture the human Crichton?

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:15.310
You can't make me.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.370
Listen, Tiana, it is the only way.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.250
Why do you care? You will be dead.

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:25.300
You are the only one of us who the peacekeepers do not hunt.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:28.230
I went down to their base with Crichton. They know who I am.

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:29.970
That is why you must wear these.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:36.470
restraints i doubt i'll be able to subdue them with those when they bought moya lock yourself in

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:40.910
one of the cells slip these on and maintain no matter how many times they asked that we forced

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:45.810
you to help don't tell me how to lie it's one of the best things i do you are a real pain in the

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:59.530
joy exactly how volatile is this lutrol not at all

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:03.450
But once it's injected into containers filled with cronite,

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:06.870
shavings from the floor of Moyer's cargo hold,

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:09.620
the mix becomes highly explosive.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:12.730
Almost anything will set it off.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.660
Say, like, high-speed impact?

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:21.100
Are you sure there's no other way?

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:26.280
Oh, yeah.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:29.440
Now the tools of the chief anarchist.

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:38.280
John made a new family here surrounded by all of you.

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:40.500
Now I sense it's coming to an end.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:44.480
Well, it's a Jerry Springer kind of family.

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:50.720
But for what it's worth, Zan, you are family.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.980
I appreciate your concern, Officer Sun, but I no longer require...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:10.000
a chaperone. Are you sure, Pilot? You seem quite upset. Yes. Moya is terrified for her offspring

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:18.280
and herself. That anxiety translates through her being into mine. Combine it with my own fear,

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:27.400
and... Pretty potent adrenaline surge for you, I understand. Officer Sun.

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:38.590
Aaron, you and I, we've shared quite a lot in the time we've been together.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:44.620
DNA for one. Help me learn some rudimentary science.

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:54.520
You've kept me alive when no one else could. There's no reason we all need to be recaptured.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:57.240
Have your prowler.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:02.860
I don't think that option hasn't entered my mind.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:09.100
I'm not going anywhere.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:19.350
Maya wants to know, have you come up with a name for her offspring yet?

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.560
In case something happens.

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:26.250
She doesn't want her son named by the peacekeepers.

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:36.720
Please tell Moya that it remains my honor to name her son.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:48.780
It will be a good, strong name that he will bear proudly in freedom if I have anything to say about it.

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:53.800
Tell her.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:10:59.800
Toward that end.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:05.120
And we need the DRDs to start scoping cronite shavings from the cargo holds.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:19.480
This is probably the last note in the bottle you're going to get.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:29.970
Things have gone bad here and, uh, why don't I just start screaming and leave them a real...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:47.850
happy memory see anything like the man I met oh no no no no the man you met was

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:52.530
an alien and taking the form of my father but he was constructed from your

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:59.500
memory so was it accurate no idealized but mostly yeah

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:02.910
You're lucky, you know.

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:09.330
When I was very young one night,

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:12.980
a soldier appeared over my bunk,

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:16.960
a little hardened, scarred.

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:18.840
Cool. Your father?

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:19.560
My mother.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:23.530
She told me that I wasn't merely an accident

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:26.030
or a genetic birthing to fill the ranks,

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:29.980
that she and a male that she had cared about...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.550
had chosen to heal the knife. Mine.

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:37.760
What about your father? I know even less.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:49.560
Leave him a message. You don't even know.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:38.320
You have eaten. You have bathed.

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:41.540
What next? A nap?

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:43.700
Hmm. As a matter of fact, uh...

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:48.430
We must talk about your future.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:52.760
Tch! You're clearly not the one to decide my future, Kreis.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:53.660
What do you mean?

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:56.000
Well, you've lost control here, haven't you?

00:13:56.790 --> 00:13:59.980
Not that it troubles me, but this Scorpius fellow...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.130
He's obviously the one in power now

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:03.850
Be that as it may

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:08.890
Allow me to make a case for my value in these negotiations

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:10.720
Your Highness

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:22.430
Do you know what this is?

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:23.730
You madman

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:25.330
This is your death certificate

00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:26.550
Proof you expired

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:27.460
You're early

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:28.880
Come back tomorrow

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:29.970
I am

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.190
I'm not your reaper, Scorpiuses.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:37.180
Did you really think you could strike an honest bargain with a scarring half-breed like him?

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:42.280
The moment Crichton is in custody, he's ordered your execution to show everyone what he thinks of traitors.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:45.670
Slow death.

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:51.750
Why tell me?

00:14:52.730 --> 00:14:57.020
Because ironically, we find ourselves in similar situations.

00:14:57.240 --> 00:14:59.900
But what I do...

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:05.390
I have no life beyond court-martial, incarceration, execution.

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:11.780
So what do you want to survive as you do?

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:14.080
And just how do we do that?

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:17.960
What is he doing back?

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:20.260
We know what he's doing back. It's a trap.

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:22.330
He was assuring pilot that it wasn't.

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:23.230
And you believe him?

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:24.700
Well, he wasn't followed.

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:28.330
Which makes no sense. This is definitely a trap.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:29.970
I wouldn't just let Nigel go.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:30.820
I'm sure of that.

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:33.480
Given provocation, I will shoot him in such a way

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:35.900
that he still is able to answer all your questions.

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:40.720
Peacekeeper tailships.

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:42.500
So far.

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:46.860
Moya's senses detect no military activity directed towards us.

00:15:47.390 --> 00:15:55.280
Please don't shoot.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:59.980
Of course, I would have demanded the same precautions myself, but...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.840
Off the throne, Sled Rydal, and face down on the ground.

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:03.660
Well, hardly.

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:06.200
Then I'd miss your reaction to whatever's about to happen.

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:11.800
And please, whatever your reaction, don't let it include weapons fire.

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:28.940
This is clearly an awkward situation.

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:36.920
However, I have asked Dominar Rigel XVI for asylum, and he has accepted.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:38.800
By the goddess, that's insane.

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:41.280
What do you need asylum from?

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:47.700
Before I can answer your questions, I would feel safer in protective custody, with passion's karma.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:48.860
Protective custody.

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:52.460
Pilot, have the DRDs checked the transport for tracking devices?

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:53.220
At once.

00:16:54.060 --> 00:16:56.780
Kiana, reinstate the cell door functions on Tier VII.

00:16:56.840 --> 00:16:57.620
With pleasure.

00:16:59.600 --> 00:16:59.880
Mood.

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:02.720
As you can see, I am unarmed.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:11.120
As you can see, I am also unarmed.

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:20.050
Oh, I said you wanted to kill me.

00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:22.290
You knew.

00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:24.610
Well along.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:33.660
Cardago did not commit the crime that he was in prison for.

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:38.880
His mate was killed by someone else.

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:43.380
Her own brother, a peacekeeper.

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:46.920
You knew, and you kept him in chains.

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:53.980
No matter what I knew, a tribunal order can release a convicted murderer.

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:55.260
Easy answer.

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:58.570
There isn't much in life that is unfair.

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:04.430
We are all proof of that.

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:08.460
If life was fair, you'd be dead.

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:26.150
So, is there anything you want to say to me?

00:18:26.470 --> 00:18:29.330
I think we covered it all when you left me for dead in the Aurora chair.

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:35.370
Good. I'm going to go and check out their transport. I still don't trust either of them.

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:58.450
What are you doing here, Chris? Really?

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:04.260
I believe my best chance is to let the Hainerian explain my position to you.

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:06.970
You're letting Rigel be your advocate?

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:11.180
You're worse off than you look.

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:15.970
If you'd have seen Kreis aboard his own ship, you'd know it was no act.

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:20.230
This Scorpius character is carrying Kreis' mivongs around in his hip pocket.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:23.440
So you decided to take pity on poor Captain Kreis.

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:26.710
I don't take pity on orphans, much less that butcher.

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:29.980
However, as the minded engineer at our original...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:37.280
escape and virtually every correct decision since then i recognize his value like chris is really

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:42.740
going to help us no choice is a walking corpse on his own ship all the more reason why scorpius

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:48.040
would not let him go again for the tiny part of your brain that calculates strategy we didn't

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:54.340
present it that way chris told scorpius that if he came here under a flag of truce he'd be able

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:58.990
to convince you all to surrender so chris must know what they're planning be useful

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:04.600
Possibly. Something went wrong.

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:08.540
You weren't there to sell us out, Nigel.

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:10.420
You bet your shiny blue ass I did.

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:13.990
But I didn't, so make the most of it now.

00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:20.780
Xan, do I inject the catalyst into every one of these cronite shaving containers or only the first row?

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:24.390
She didn't say.

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:28.640
She doesn't even know.

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:39.970
Targo, there won't be much time later.

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:41.740
I know.

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:48.410
We've had our differences, but you've become someone I rely on now.

00:20:49.960 --> 00:20:51.420
You've become similarly affected.

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:57.600
Sorry I didn't get a chance to meet your son, Jothy.

00:20:58.080 --> 00:20:59.420
I miss being a part of his life.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:05.440
each day. Your blood runs through him, Dargo. That's influence enough. I'm sure he's very much

00:21:05.440 --> 00:21:21.200
like you. Hopefully his mother's nose. Thought I would live much longer. I never thought I'd live

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:21.640
this long.

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:34.720
Report, Lieutenant.

00:21:35.700 --> 00:21:40.800
As the vector narrows, our search team is confident of locating the Leviathan within several odds.

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:42.880
Excellent, Lieutenant. Keep me informed.

